    1. Place 3-5 non-overlapping solid RED rectangles (w 1-4, h 2-6) on a 10x10 BLACK grid
    2. Ensure at least 2 pairs have horizontally-separated columns with overlapping row spans (bridgeable pairs)
    3. Run the solver (pairwise gap-fill with blocking check) to compute bridges
    4. Verify at least 1 bridge is painted and all bridge regions were originally BLACK
    5. The input is the grid before bridge painting; the output includes MAROON bridges
